{"linguistic_realization": {"reason": "Mostly fluent, but the mass paragraph contains a genuinely confusing double clause—'sitting at the high end of the qcd range, and also at the low end of the qcd range'—which is hard to parse even accounting for the position/physics distinction, and 'pushes towards top, while at the same time pushing away from top' reads as contradictory on first pass. These impede smooth reading.", "evidence": "This high mass, sitting at the high end of the qcd range, and also at the low end of the qcd range, is characteristic of a heavy particle decay depositing its products in a single jet. Its contribution of 2.27 pushes towards top, while at the same time pushing away from top,", "score": 1},
"internal_consistency": {"reason": "The mass paragraph contains a same-frame contradiction: the value is said to sit both at the high end and the low end of the qcd range, and its contribution is said to push towards top and away from top simultaneously. It also calls the value 'unusual' with rarity 4.52 and then immediately calls it 'entirely ordinary and unremarkable', directly clashing.", "evidence": "with a rarity of 4.52 it is unusual for qcd jets, which makes it an entirely ordinary and unremarkable value", "score": 0},
"overall_satisfaction": {"reason": "The narrative covers the score standing, reconstruction quality, ranked drivers, directions, and rarity for most observables, giving a generally useful account. However the badly garbled leading-observable (mass) passage undermines the reader's ability to trust or parse the single most important contribution, weakening overall understanding.", "evidence": "", "score": 1}}

{"linguistic_realization": {"reason": "The text is grammatical overall but has some awkward, telegraphic phrasing ('with rarity 4.52 it unusual for qcd jets', 'which high for qcd jets', 'sitting at high end qcd range') that reads as stitched-together fragments rather than natural prose. These recur throughout, mildly impeding smooth reading despite being understandable.", "evidence": "", "score": 2},
"internal_consistency": {"reason": "Contributions point both toward top and toward qcd across observables, which is expected and not contradictory; position vs. physics frame uses of 'high'/'low' are consistently applied per observable without same-frame clashes. The reconstruction percentile (54, 'better than most') aligns with the stated reconstructed score of 3.53 vs actual 4.1, so no clash with prior claims.", "evidence": "", "score": 3},
"overall_satisfaction": {"reason": "The narrative covers the decision, percentile standing, reconstruction adequacy, ranks observables by contribution weight, and gives rarity/interpretive framing for each major driver, giving a reasonably full interpretive account. It is somewhat flat in style (per-observable recitation) but does fulfill (a)-(d) and provides some interpretive framing (e), landing just short of the most polished narratives.", "evidence": "", "score": 2}}
